# --- s035 Book I d.8 q.3 = Ord. I d.8 p.1 q.3 (Vat. IV)
n("n589","s035-01","Tertia questio octaue distinctionis","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 3 (ed. Vat. IV), *utrum Deus vel aliquid formaliter dictum de Deo sit in genere*. Scotus's important discussion of univocity and the intrinsic modes falls here.","certain")
n("n590","s035-01","Auic. 2°. metha. c. 1.","la","source","Avicenna, *Liber de philosophia prima* II c. 1: the division of being into *in subiecto* and *non in subiecto*, with substance as the latter. This is the standard citation in *Ord.* I d. 8.","to-verify")
n("n591","s035-01","remouentur a deo illa predicata artis dyaletice","la","source","The thought (the categories of the *ars dialectica* fail when applied to God) is Boethius's (*De Trinitate* c. 4: *cuncta mutantur, cum quis in divinam vertit praedicationem*) rather than Augustine's (cf. *De Trin.* V 1.2–2.3). Unidentified as an Augustinian quotation.","to-verify")
n("n592","s035-02","opinio Henrici in summa arti. 22.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Summa quaestionum ordinariarum* a. 21–22 (analogy of being: no concept common to God and creatures). Scotus attacks this opinion at *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 1 qq. 1–2 and d. 8 p. 1 q. 3.","to-verify")
n("n593","s035-02","Henricus est quodlibeto. 10. q. 7.","la","source","Henry, *Quodl.* X q. 7. Gorris's identification of the *responsio aliquorum* (on *ens ratum*) is to be checked against the Vatican apparatus.","to-verify")
n("n594","s035-02","tacta est superius di. 3. q. 1.","la","source","The ‘certain/doubtful concept’ argument for univocity: *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 1 qq. 1–2 n. 27 (*omnis intellectus certus de uno conceptu et dubius de diversis…*), repeated in d. 8 p. 1 q. 3. Gorris's cross-reference is correct.","certain")
n("n595","s035-02","Johannis Roditori li. 1. di. 2. q. 6.","la","historical","John of Rodington again (cf. §s031-02), here *Roditori*, I d. 2 q. 6, credited with the ‘disjunctive certainty’ reply. To be checked.","to-verify")
n("n596","s035-03","Alberti de Saxonia et fratris Roberti de Olcot. libro primo q. 5.","la","source","Robert Holcot OP, *In quattuor libros Sententiarum quaestiones*, I q. 5, is plausible (Holcot's *Sentences* is arranged in questions). Albert of Saxony (d. 1390) wrote no known *Sentences* commentary. Either Gorris refers to a logical work of his, or *Alberti* stands for another author. To be checked.","to-verify")
n("n597","s035-03","q. 3. articulo. 5.","la","source","Aquinas, *ST* I q. 3 a. 5, *utrum Deus sit in aliquo genere*.","certain")
n("n598","s035-04","in illo libello","la","source","Boethius, *De Trinitate* c. 4–5: substance and relation are the two ways of predicating in God (*duo modi praedicandi*). *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 3 discusses the Boethian authority.","to-verify")
n("n599","s035-04","Aug. 7. de tri. c. 8.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* VII 5.10: God is called *substantia* only *abusive*, since *substare* implies the bearing of accidents (*abusive substantiam vocari*).","certain")
n("n600","s035-04","Auic. 8. metha. c. 10.","la","source","Avicenna, *Liber de philosophia prima* VIII c. 4: the First has no genus. The chapter number *10* is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n601","s035-06","in albedine habente decem gradus","la","source","Scotus's example of a whiteness with ten degrees: genus and difference taken from distinct *realitates* of one thing. Cf. *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 3 nn. 106–108 (*realitas a qua sumitur genus… realitas a qua sumitur differentia*).","to-verify")
n("n602","s035-07","gracia materie","la","translation","*gratia materiae* = ‘for the sake of the example’ (lit. ‘for the matter's sake’), a scholastic formula.")
n("n603","s035-02","ratified being","en","translation","*ens ratum*: Henry of Ghent's *esse ratum*, the ‘ratified’ or certified being of an essence.")
n("n604","s035-02","Solemn Doctor","en","translation","*doctor solennis*: Henry of Ghent's customary epithet.")
n("n605","s035-03","Robert Holcot","en","translation","Lat. *Roberti de Olcot*.")

